# Collision shapes
@scenario tutorial_lesson_26
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide listen]
pip: A visible shape can have different bounds from its collision shape.
pip: In the JES editor, use the example panel as a reference. Compare its drawn bounds with the collision shape you would give it.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: What determines whether two physical objects can collide?
> Their displayed colors. -> retry
> Their physics bodies and collision shapes. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: Visual bounds and collision shapes serve different purposes. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: Visual bounds and collision shapes serve different purposes.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_26]
[flag tutorial_done_26]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_5]
